Guys, Senator Kamala Harris
is a senator

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
from the great state
of California.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
I got to talk to her today.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Here is my chat
with Senator Kamala Harris.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.512
Senator Harris,
thank you so much

00:00:01.512 --> 00:00:03.814
for being on "The Tonight Show"
and coming back to us.

00:00:03.814 --> 00:00:06.584
-Thanks.
-I know these are
very difficult times

00:00:06.584 --> 00:00:08.219
and you're very,
very busy right now,

00:00:08.219 --> 00:00:10.220
so I really, really
appreciate this. Thank you.

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:13.224
Thank you so much for this.
-Good to be with you again.

00:00:13.224 --> 00:00:15.259
-If you don't mind,
I'd like to get right to --

00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:16.893
the breaking news today
was that

00:00:16.893 --> 00:00:19.563
the three
other officers involved

00:00:19.563 --> 00:00:24.568
with the death of George Floyd
have now been charged.

00:00:24.568 --> 00:00:25.836
What are your thoughts?

00:00:25.836 --> 00:00:30.841
-As of today, we're one
step closer to justice.

00:00:30.841 --> 00:00:32.509
But, you know,
I have long believed

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:34.044
and I think we all know,

00:00:34.044 --> 00:00:37.014
"Justice delayed
is justice denied."

00:00:37.014 --> 00:00:39.717
And why it has to take so long

00:00:39.717 --> 00:00:43.587
for those other three officers
to be held accountable.

00:00:43.587 --> 00:00:46.723
It has, you know, caused pain
for Mr. Floyd's family

00:00:46.723 --> 00:00:47.892
and the community

00:00:47.892 --> 00:00:50.094
and all of us
who watched that video

00:00:50.094 --> 00:00:52.229
and are watching
what's happening.

00:00:52.229 --> 00:00:54.598
But, thankfully, Keith Ellison,
the attorney general,

00:00:54.598 --> 00:00:58.535
has taken over the case and is
obviously not wasting any time

00:00:58.535 --> 00:01:02.706
in making sure that justice is
delivered to Mr. Floyd's family

00:01:02.706 --> 00:01:06.577
and to that community
and to our country.

00:01:06.577 --> 00:01:09.013
-What are your thoughts on the
administration currently

00:01:09.013 --> 00:01:11.882
and how they've been dealing
with this,

00:01:11.882 --> 00:01:15.318
on top of the pandemic?

00:01:15.318 --> 00:01:16.520
-I mean, Jimmy,

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:19.856
we've got a president
of the United States,

00:01:19.856 --> 00:01:22.593
or, at least, somebody
who occupies that position,

00:01:22.593 --> 00:01:25.162
who doesn't understand the job

00:01:25.162 --> 00:01:27.097
and isn't capable
of performing the job.

00:01:27.097 --> 00:01:30.167
And, most recently,
you know, frankly,

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.803
the words that he speaks are
the words, not of a president.

00:01:32.803 --> 00:01:35.639
They're the words of a dictator.

00:01:35.639 --> 00:01:37.040
I was in D.C. that night.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.443
You know, I joined
the protesters in D.C.

00:01:39.443 --> 00:01:40.844
-I saw that.
-So I've been out there,

00:01:40.844 --> 00:01:44.081
you know, and I will tell you
that, had my parents

00:01:44.081 --> 00:01:46.283
not marched and shouted
in the '60s,

00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:50.087
I would not have been,
together with all those who did,

00:01:50.087 --> 00:01:53.090
I'm pretty certain that I would
not be talking with you tonight

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.325
as only the second Black woman

00:01:54.325 --> 00:01:57.361
ever elected to the
United States Senate.

00:01:57.361 --> 00:02:00.531
There are so many things
that we, as a society,

00:02:00.531 --> 00:02:04.301
have benefited from because
people took to the streets

00:02:04.301 --> 00:02:06.837
to exercise their
First Amendment right

00:02:06.837 --> 00:02:09.740
to speak out
and speak to their government

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:11.641
so that we could see progress.

00:02:11.641 --> 00:02:15.545
And the idea that,
just a couple of nights ago,

00:02:15.545 --> 00:02:18.281
this guy, Donald Trump,
who happens to, right now,

00:02:18.281 --> 00:02:19.750
be president
of the United States,

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:27.324
would throw tear gas at people
who are peacefully protesting

00:02:27.324 --> 00:02:30.460
-Oof!
-so he could clear the roads!

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.297
Right? It reminds me
of the emperor with no clothes.

00:02:33.297 --> 00:02:38.769
So he could clear the roads,
to walk!

00:02:38.769 --> 00:02:43.774
To carry the Bible,
the Holy Bible.

00:02:43.774 --> 00:02:47.444
You know, it is as though
it were one of his steaks,

00:02:47.444 --> 00:02:48.979
one of his Trump steaks...

00:02:48.979 --> 00:02:52.115
-[ Laughs ]
-...for a photo op.

00:02:52.115 --> 00:02:55.018
And, that night, 'cause I was
at my apartment in D.C.,

00:02:55.018 --> 00:02:58.455
I heard the Black Hawks flying.

00:02:58.455 --> 00:03:00.690
You know, the last time
I was on a Black Hawk?

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.927
When I was in Afghanistan.

00:03:02.927 --> 00:03:04.061
-Wow!

00:03:04.061 --> 00:03:08.365
-These are military aircraft

00:03:08.365 --> 00:03:13.670
that are being turned
on the people of America.

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:17.141
He's talking about turning
the U.S. military

00:03:17.141 --> 00:03:20.110
on its own people.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:22.079
I serve on the Senate
Intelligence Committee.

00:03:22.079 --> 00:03:25.181
I serve on the
Homeland Security Committee.

00:03:25.181 --> 00:03:29.954
This is not the America
that people fought for

00:03:29.954 --> 00:03:33.824
and this is not the America that
is the America of our ideals.

00:03:33.824 --> 00:03:35.392
This is something altogether,

00:03:35.392 --> 00:03:39.063
and that's why people
are marching and shouting.

00:03:39.063 --> 00:03:41.799
And the optimism that I have

00:03:41.799 --> 00:03:43.534
is the optimism
that all of us have

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.902
whenever we are
in these kinds of fights,

00:03:45.902 --> 00:03:47.670
which is it's not a fight
against something.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.873
It's fight for something.

00:03:49.873 --> 00:03:51.942
But, you know...
-Wow.

00:03:51.942 --> 00:03:53.310
-...Donald Trump doesn't get it

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:56.480
and that's why everyone's
gotta make sure

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.716
that we vote in November

00:03:58.716 --> 00:04:05.021
and show ourselves and the world
that we are better than this.

00:04:05.021 --> 00:04:06.957
-Speaking of November...

00:04:06.957 --> 00:04:08.325
-Mm-hmm.
-...I've seen you in

00:04:08.325 --> 00:04:10.327
numerous interviews,
saying that

00:04:10.327 --> 00:04:12.897
it's gonna be
a very important time

00:04:12.897 --> 00:04:13.931
in our history.
-Uh-huh.

00:04:13.931 --> 00:04:15.299
Yes, it will be.

00:04:15.299 --> 00:04:18.268
-What are we looking at, here,
in November, coming up?

00:04:18.268 --> 00:04:19.736
-Okay, so, first of all,

00:04:19.736 --> 00:04:21.705
there's so much at stake
in the election.

00:04:21.705 --> 00:04:23.674
I mean, so, again,
we're in the midst

00:04:23.674 --> 00:04:27.043
of a public health --
we're in a pandemic.

00:04:27.043 --> 00:04:30.981
We have had over 100,000 souls,

00:04:30.981 --> 00:04:35.252
in just less than 100 days,
perish, die, right?

00:04:35.252 --> 00:04:38.522
Millions of people
have contracted this virus

00:04:38.522 --> 00:04:42.993
and are suffering in its grip.

00:04:42.993 --> 00:04:48.198
We have over 40 million people
who were working,

00:04:48.198 --> 00:04:50.000
who are now unemployed,

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:54.271
just in the last 100 days,
because of this pandemic.

00:04:54.271 --> 00:04:56.606
And one of the things that --

00:04:56.606 --> 00:04:59.309
One, I will again say that

00:04:59.309 --> 00:05:02.579
we would not be in as bad
of a situation as we are,

00:05:02.579 --> 00:05:04.748
had the president
not taken immediate action,

00:05:04.748 --> 00:05:06.750
had the president
not called it a hoax

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:09.986
and minimized
the seriousness of it.

00:05:09.986 --> 00:05:11.288
And we are where we are.

00:05:11.288 --> 00:05:13.424
So, in terms of the election,

00:05:13.424 --> 00:05:15.192
one of the things
that we have to make sure

00:05:15.192 --> 00:05:18.328
is that people can go
and vote and be safe.

00:05:18.328 --> 00:05:20.164
So, I have a proposal.

00:05:20.164 --> 00:05:22.532
I call it the Vote Safe Act,

00:05:22.532 --> 00:05:24.835
that basically is
that states should have --

00:05:24.835 --> 00:05:27.471
all states should have
vote by mail.

00:05:27.471 --> 00:05:29.173
All states should
have early voting,

00:05:29.173 --> 00:05:30.774
at least 20 days
before Election Day,

00:05:30.774 --> 00:05:33.777
so you can figure out when
it works for you to go vote.

00:05:33.777 --> 00:05:36.179
And all states should also,
for people who do go

00:05:36.179 --> 00:05:38.615
to the polls,
have safety precautions,

00:05:38.615 --> 00:05:41.685
things like curbside voting,
or put in place wait times,

00:05:41.685 --> 00:05:43.220
so that, unlike in Wisconsin,

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:45.255
people stood in line
for two to three hours,

00:05:45.255 --> 00:05:46.857
people would only have
to stand in line

00:05:46.857 --> 00:05:48.492
for a certain number of minutes.

00:05:48.492 --> 00:05:50.661
So, these are some of the things
that I'm fighting for.

00:05:50.661 --> 00:05:54.431
In terms of this BS about fraud,

00:05:54.431 --> 00:05:57.601
listen, Donald Trump spoke
the quiet words out loud

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:58.935
when he said

00:05:58.935 --> 00:06:02.373
that he was concerned that he
and the Republican Party

00:06:02.373 --> 00:06:05.376
would lose,
if people vote by mail.

00:06:05.376 --> 00:06:09.113
Meanwhile, he himself, and I
believe family members of him,

00:06:09.113 --> 00:06:12.683
have voted by mail consistently.

00:06:12.683 --> 00:06:15.619
So, the whole thing about fraud
in the vote-by-mail system

00:06:15.619 --> 00:06:20.724
is really a red herring
to distract people

00:06:20.724 --> 00:06:23.093
from the seriousness
of this moment,

00:06:23.093 --> 00:06:24.861
which is that we're
in the middle of a pandemic.

00:06:24.861 --> 00:06:27.497
We want people to be able
to be safe when they vote

00:06:27.497 --> 00:06:29.466
and we definitely
wanna make sure

00:06:29.466 --> 00:06:31.101
that people don't have
to make a choice

00:06:31.101 --> 00:06:34.370
between their health and their
right to exercise their voice,

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.641
especially at this moment
in time in our country.

